<main class="container section"><div class="section-head"><span class="number">06 / LEGAL</span><h2>Privacy.</h2></div><p class="intro">This page describes how information submitted through this website is handled. Only information needed to respond to enquiries, process book enquiries, secure the administration area, or operate the site should be collected.</p><div class="legal-copy"><h3>Information you provide</h3><p>Contact and book-enquiry forms may collect your name, email address, message or order notes, and the information needed to respond to your request. This information is used for the purpose for which you provide it and is not intentionally collected beyond that purpose.</p><h3>Security information</h3><p>Administrative sign-in attempts may be recorded with the source IP address, email address, success status, and timestamp. This security log is used to detect and limit abusive login activity and protect the administration area. Security records should be retained only as long as reasonably necessary for that purpose.</p><h3>Cookies and sessions</h3><p>The site may use a session cookie for normal application features such as the book enquiry cart, CSRF protection, and authenticated administration. These sessions are used to maintain application state and security rather than for advertising.</p><h3>Third parties</h3><p>The public engineering activity section may request public repository information from GitHub. No private repository credentials are required by the website for that display.</p><h3>Data security</h3><p>Reasonable technical controls are used to protect submitted information, including input validation, CSRF protection, secure session handling, and database access controls. No internet-facing system can guarantee absolute security, so unnecessary sensitive information should not be submitted through public forms.</p></div></main>
